3482   E36D             
3483   E36D             ;This is unused in the macros. You must call it directly at $F1D5
3484   E36D             ;The behavior of this command is probably the most complex. It 
3485   E36D             ;starts at the last lamp in the range. If it is already set, then
3486   E36D             ;the routine simply exits. If the last lamp is not set, the routine
3487   E36D             ;goes down through each lamp in the range. If if finds a lamp on,
3488   E36D             ;then it turns off that lamp, then goes back up to the next lamp
3489   E36D             ;and turns it on. If no lamps are on in the range, then the first
3490   E36D             ;lamp in the range is turned on.
3491   E36D             ;The best example of this routine is for the 10-20-30 lamps on 
3492   E36D             ;Jungle Lord. It will simply incrment the 10-20-30 lamps sequentially
3493   E36D             ;and then stop at 30. If none are on, then it will turn on 10.
3494   E36D             lampm_g             
3495   E36D 8D 4F                       bsr lampr_end               ;A = Last Lamp Level, B = Last Lamp BitPos
3496   E36F 26 3A                       bne abx_ret
