5691   F015             ;**********************************************************************************
5692   F015             ;* NMI Routines - This section of code is run only when the 
5693   F015             ;*                diagnostic switch on the CPU board is pressed.
5694   F015             ;*                It will test the hardware and report any errors
5695   F015             ;*                via the LED display on the CPU board. If all tests
5696   F015             ;*                are passed, the LED display will show '0' and
5697   F015             ;*                the code jumps to the normal power-up routines.
5698   F015             ;*
5699   F015             ;* Errors are as Follows:
5700   F015             ;*
5701   F015             ;*      0 - Test Passed
5702   F015             ;*      1 - IC13 RAM Fault (Most Significant Nybble)
5703   F015             ;*      2 - IC16 RAM Fault (Least Significant Nybble)
5704   F015             ;*      3 - IC17 ROM 2 Fault (Location $F000-$FFFF)
5705   F015             ;*      4 - IC14 ROM 1 Fault (Location $E000-$EFFF)
5706   F015             ;*      5 - IC20 ROM 0 Fault (Location $D000-$DFFF)
5707   F015             ;*      6 - Not Used
5708   F015             ;*      7 - Not Used
5709   F015             ;*      8 - IC19 CMOS RAM Fault or Memory Protect Failure
5710   F015             ;*      9 - Coin Door Closed or Memory Protect Failure or IC19 CMOS RAM Fault
5711   F015             ;**********************************************************************************
